Group 1 – CDA Readiness and Resilience
Ingestion, schema compatibility, resource failures, network failures, retries, idempotency and performance.
Execute mainly before production cutover, in a controlled test environment.




Group 2 – CDA Switchover Execution
ADF deactivation and activation, existing ODS object renaming, new view creation, data reconciliation and downstream Silver validation.
Execute in the switchover rehearsal and appropriate production cutover checks.




Group 3 – CDC and Data Continuity
Insert, Update, Hard Delete, same-day transactions, SCD current flags, changes around switchover and subsequent incremental loads.
Validate during the rehearsal and after switchover.




Group 4 – CDA Rollback
Stop CDA downstream jobs, restore RR ODS tables/views and original ADF pipelines, restart from the previous watermark, validate catch-up and reconcile Silver.
Execute as a separate controlled rollback rehearsal.
